+# Current native design
+
+The reviewed period-2/3 prototype remains the source of those programs. A thin
+adapter exposes `native.py`, which adds a third, genuinely dependent rule:
+first eastward gray hit -> four-connected component -> cardinality -> spacing
+of cardinality plus one -> marker-relative lattice filling. An actual selected
+component of size five gives spacing six. Substituting a different component's
+size changes the final output; both programs are retained in a protected-Racket
+causal witness after native qualification.
+
+The sampler is shared across settings and constructs a minimum teaching core
+before adding independently counted demonstrations and queries. A compact
+pentomino separates component size from bbox height plus width, an equivalence
+found during independent review of the initial L-shaped design. The guard also
+tests first/last/nearest selection, four/eight connectivity, row-run length,
+bbox area and lattice shortcuts. No claim of uniqueness beyond these rivals.
+
+Keep canonical generation/authority unchanged; extend sizes only in this native
+family. Use 3 demos ordinarily (supported 2–6), 4 novel queries, exact native
+source qualification and one counterfactual witness. Reuse the existing public
+byte/ID helper. Do not add a controller, model training or approval shortcuts.
+
+Implementation and checks are in `native.py`, `adapter.py`, `promotion.json`,
+`verify_native.py` and the task tests. Current evidence paths and limitations are
+in `README.md`, the native inventory and the packet results.
+
